 "blocks": {
  "af7dcb00731f9c01": {
   "type": "terms",
   "items": [
    {
     "term": "session",
     "md": "One running omp or pi agent with the extension loaded; it has a callsign such as `be-audio-001`."
    },
    {
     "term": "collective",
     "md": "Every session in one omp profile (`~/.agent-collective/<profile>/`). The TUI never shows another profile."
    },
    {
     "term": "contact",
     "md": "A session this one has messaged or heard from; starred and listed first."
    },
    {
     "term": "offline",
     "md": "A callsign still reserved for a session that is not running (up to 7 days after it last ran)."
    },
    {
     "term": "thread",
     "md": "The messages this session exchanged with one peer, oldest first."
    }
   ]
  },
  "810fc0fb8673777e": {
   "type": "checklist",
   "id": "brief",
   "title": "Picks",
   "numbered": false,
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "framework",
     "text": "Which framework do the screens use?",
     "sub": "Recommend Plain kit: these are terminal cells, so only colour tokens and a monospace grid matter.",
     "recommend": "plain",
     "choices": [
      {
       "id": "plain",
       "label": "Plain kit"
      },
      {
       "id": "horizon",
       "label": "HorizonUI"
      }
     ],
     "detail": "The real UI is drawn by omp's TUI (`Component.render(width) → string[]`) and by Tern's TSP nodes (`tern.ui.table`, `list`, `badge`), not by HTML. The mock only needs a character grid and the theme's colours; a component framework would mislead about what can be drawn."
    },
    {
     "id": "theme",
     "text": "Which theme?",
     "sub": "Recommend omp dark: it is what the overlay sits on; Tern re-skins its block with its own theme anyway.",
     "recommend": "omp-dark",
     "choices": [
      {
       "id": "omp-dark",
       "label": "omp dark"
      },
      {
       "id": "tern",
       "label": "Tern"
      },
      {
       "id": "light",
       "label": "Light terminal"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "omp-layout",
     "text": "Choose how /collective opens in omp and pi",
     "sub": "Recommend full-screen overlay: 25 sessions need the rows; Esc returns to the transcript.",
     "recommend": "full",
     "choices": [
      {
       "id": "full",
       "label": "Full-screen overlay"
      },
      {
       "id": "panel",
       "label": "Bottom panel (12 rows)"
      }
     ],
     "detail": "Full-screen: the **Sessions** and **Thread** screens. Bottom panel: the **Sessions, bottom panel** variant; the transcript stays visible above, 8 sessions fit before scrolling, and the thread opens full-screen anyway."
    },
    {
     "id": "message-log",
     "text": "Decide whether each session keeps a message log",
     "sub": "Recommend log: the thread view and outcome history need it; cost is one small file append per message.",
     "recommend": "log",
     "choices": [
      {
       "id": "log",
       "label": "Keep a log"
      },
      {
       "id": "none",
       "label": "No log"
      }
     ],
     "detail": "**Keep a log:** append one JSON line per sent or received message to `sessions/<session-id>.log.jsonl` (time, peer, direction, hop, outcome, body), capped at the last 500 lines. **No log:** the Thread screen can show only messages that arrived since the TUI opened; outcomes of earlier sends are lost."
    },
    {
     "id": "offline-rows",
     "text": "Decide whether offline callsigns appear in the list",
     "sub": "Recommend show, dimmed: a send to them is answered \"offline\" anyway, so seeing them avoids the surprise.",
     "recommend": "show",
     "choices": [
      {
       "id": "show",
       "label": "Show, dimmed"
      },
      {
       "id": "toggle",
       "label": "Hidden, `o` shows"
      },
      {
       "id": "hide",
       "label": "Never show"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "tern-send",
     "text": "Choose how the Tern block sends a message",
     "sub": "Recommend a CLI in the package: Tern plugins can run processes but cannot open unix sockets.",
     "recommend": "cli",
     "choices": [
      {
       "id": "cli",
       "label": "agent-collective send CLI"
      },
      {
       "id": "focus-only",
       "label": "Go to pane only"
      }
     ],
     "detail": "Tern's Luau API has `tern.fs` (read records) and `tern.process.run`, but no socket client. **CLI:** ship `bin/agent-collective send <callsign> <message>` in the package; the block runs it, and the peer sees the message as from `you (via Tern)` at hop 0. **Go to pane only:** the block lists sessions and jumps to their pane; you type there."
    }
   ]
  },
  "15befa216d4ee87b": {
   "type": "text",
   "md": "**Who:** you, running 5–30 sessions across worktrees, up to 3 per directory. **Where:** inside an omp or pi terminal (`/collective` opens it with `ctx.ui.custom`, both hosts support it), or as a Tern pane when the sessions run in Tern.\n\nEach screen must let you:\n\n- **Sessions:** see every session in the profile with its state (working, idle, quiet, offline), directory and harness. Also where it runs (Tern pane, herdr pane or tty); filter by text; star contacts first.\n- **Thread:** read what this session and one peer said, with each delivery's outcome (woken, aside, coalesced, refused) and hop; write a message and send it.\n- **Tern block:** the same list as a native Tern block, plus *go to pane*, because Tern knows where each session's pane is.\n\nAll data comes from files the extension already writes: records (`<pid>.json`), claims (`names/`) and session state (`sessions/<id>.json`). Reading them costs no model turn and no socket traffic. Two things are new and need your pick: a per-session message log (the thread view needs it) and a way for Tern to send."
  },
